TITLE
Design Space Exploration and Ptolemy II

CHAPTER
02.cad

ABSTRACT

In todays embedded system designs, the ability to make the proper
trade-offs between the many variables involved, is increasingly
becoming the key to a successful realization. To support these
designers, we want to develop in PtolemyII a domain that supports
designers in making these trade-offs by making design space
exploration easy, thereby helping designers in posing the important
"what-if" questions and doing the analysis.

<p>

Design space exploration consists in general of selecting particular
parameter values, executing one or more models, and representing multi
dimensional information produced by the models. Also, since many
different models are created, executed, and studied, some kind of data
management needs to be available. Ptolemy II seems to be well-suited
for addressing the issues appear in design space
exploration. PtolemyII has a well-engineered software architecture,
clear defined actor model making it easy to implement and extend new
functionality, and also, the advent of the graphical front-end makes
the construction of a design space experiment easy. In developing the
design space exploration domain, much of the research time will be
devoted in how the data management needs to be integrated in the actor
model such that the overall system is robust and has multi-user and
multi-site capabilities. The later two issues are important as more
and more designs happen in teams at various places at the same time.

